    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9634" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">complōrātus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conp-</span></b> ), ūs,
			m.
		id., i. q. comploratio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a loud</i>, <i>violent
			moaning</i>, <i>lamentation</i>, etc., esp. of
			several persons (only in Liv.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">familiarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					22, 55, 7</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">23, 42, 5</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">justo conploratu prosequi mortuos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					25, 26, 10</span></i>
			.</div>
